.TH BANDWIDTH\-LOGGER 1 "2026-08-04" "bandwidth-logger 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bandwidth\-logger \- run internet speed tests on a schedule and keep a complete history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bandwidth\-logger
.RI [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bandwidth\-logger
opens the Bandwidth Logger window. It measures your internet connection at an
interval you choose and keeps a permanent, timestamped record of every test on
this computer.
.PP
The application is normally started from the application menu rather than from
a terminal, and no part of ordinary use requires a terminal or administrator
privileges.
.PP
Every attempted test produces a record, including tests that failed, timed
out, or were skipped because another test was still running. A gap in the
history therefore always has a stated reason.
.SH SCHEDULING
Automatic testing is performed by a systemd
.B user
timer, so tests continue after the window is closed and resume after you log
back in. The timer runs
.BR bandwidth-logger-run (1)
with the
.B \-\-scheduled
option.
.PP
Missed runs are never replayed. A computer that was switched off or suspended
resumes with a single test on the normal schedule, and the interruption is
recorded.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bandwidth\-logger/bandwidth\-logger.sqlite3
The authoritative record of every test, and the application's settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bandwidth\-logger/application.log
Rotating diagnostic log. Not a record of results.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/bandwidth\-logger\-test.timer
.TQ
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/bandwidth\-logger\-test.service
The user timer and service written when automatic testing is switched on.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_LOGGER_HOME
Redirects every path above beneath the named directory. Intended for testing.
.TP
.B BANDWIDTH_LOGGER_DEBUG
When set, the diagnostic log records debug-level messages.
.SH PRIVACY
Nothing is transmitted anywhere except the speed test itself, which
necessarily contacts a test server. There is no account, no cloud service, no
analytics and no telemetry. The external IP address is stored with each record
but is excluded from exported CSV files unless you ask for it.
.SH UNINSTALLING
Removing the package does not delete your records. To delete them, remove
.I ~/.local/share/bandwidth\-logger
and
.IR ~/.local/state/bandwidth\-logger .
To stop background testing first, switch Automatic testing off in the window,
or run:
.PP
.RS
systemctl \-\-user disable \-\-now bandwidth\-logger\-test.timer
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bandwidth-logger-run (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
